model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway.poolMembership {
    metadata {
      constraint "Mirror preparation before a signed native membership read tries every candidate account on its own, replacing carry 0426's rule that one failure refuses the read. Candidates mirror concurrently, at most four at a time, oldest attempt first and then by account, so an account cut off at the budget goes first on the next read. Both budgets run from the read's arrival, so they include the first locked membership read: mirrors stop at the pool's read deadline (nativeMembershipReadTimeoutMs, 10 seconds, shared through native-contract.ts) less 4 seconds, and the second locked membership read gives way at the deadline less 1 second, when the first read answers without the accounts mirrored since. With nothing newly mirrored the second read is skipped. A mirror past the budget is interrupted in the background, so its finalizers never hold the answer. An account whose mirror fails, for any cause including a defect, not answering within the budget, or being cut off before it starts, is logged with a closed reason (an acquisition reason, not_found, storage, defect or timeout), never provider text, and is left out of that read's answer, so the pool installs and serves its other accounts while the failing one is not served. An abandoned mirror keeps its pending reference for the next attempt. A failed account is skipped, and still left out, until its next attempt time: one minute after the first failure, then 2 and 4 minutes, then every 5 minutes, so an account whose backend comes back by itself is served within 5 minutes; a cut-off account is not backed off, and a new credential generation is tried at once. Every failed attempt logs one warning, the first always, with its consecutive failures, the reads that left it out since the last line, and its next wait; an account's first cut-off logs one line and later cut-offs are counted on its next line; recovery logs once when it mirrors again. A manual account check does not reach the mirror and leaves the backoff unchanged. The backoff is advisory memory per isolate, keyed on the acquisition registration and credential key that carry 0540 binds every tools gateway runtime to, so it outlives the runtime each Worker event builds; losing it costs an early retry, never a wrong answer. Leaving it out removes only its channel membership in Home; its saved account, link and credential are unchanged. The snapshot shape the pool reads is unchanged."
    }
  }
}
